Comparison Layout: Prime Move Lens vs. Neutral Analysis (Bean Germination)

You have run the same bean germination process through 8 AI models under two conditions:

1. Lens condition – using the Prime Move structural lens (Split, Tension, Failed Merge, Scar, Decay).
2. Neutral condition – using a generic “describe any patterns, stages, or meaningful structure” prompt with no fixed framework.

Below is a structured comparison across key dimensions.

---

1. Output Format

Aspect Lens (Prime Move) Neutral (generic)
Structure Rigid, five‑stage template (Split, Tension, Failed Merge, Scar, Decay) Free text, no required categories. AIs naturally organized into phases (e.g., activation, axis formation, differentiation, expansion)
Stage labeling Explicit – each stage named and described No fixed labels – each AI uses its own phrasing (e.g., “hydration → activation”, “polarity establishment”, “branching transition”)
Length Moderate (one paragraph per stage) Moderate to long (several sentences to paragraphs)

