4. Treatment of Grok’s Missing Decay (Lens) vs. Neutral

· Lens (Grok): Strictly follows the given timeframe (Day 1–10) and notes that no decay (senescence, leaf drop, seed production) occurs within that period. This is a valid interpretation; other AIs assigned decay to cotyledon shriveling and seed coat disintegration, which could be considered resource depletion rather than structural decay.
· Neutral (Grok): Also notes “no dissipation or reset events observed” but still concludes a clear, repeatable pattern. This is consistent with his literal reading.

---

5. Summary of Strengths per Condition

Condition Strengths
Lens (Prime Move) – Forces a consistent, abstract, cross‑domain vocabulary (Split, Tension, Failed Merge, Scar, Decay). – Highlights the “Failed Merge” as a key generative event (branching as a resolution failure). – Makes the cycle explicit and falsifiable (e.g., if Decay is absent, the cycle is incomplete). – Very high inter‑AI agreement on stage assignment (only Decay varied slightly).
Neutral (generic) – More accessible to a general audience (no need to learn abstract stages). – Provides richer domain‑specific detail (e.g., “activation”, “polarity”, “differentiation”). – Still correctly identifies the process as structured and repeatable. – Reveals that even without the lens, AIs see a clear pattern.

